==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ru|карандашъ}} {{ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
In Russian from the 16–17th centuries. Borrowing from a {{etyl|trk|ru}} language. Compare {{etyl|tr|-}} {{term|karataş||black slate|lang=tr}}, composed of {{term|kara||black|lang=tr}} + {{term|taş||stone|lang=tr}}, {{etyl|tt|-}} {{term|кара таш||graphite, black lead|lang=tt}}. The origin of epenthetic {{term||-н-|lang=ru}} is unclear. Perhaps it was added in colloquial Russian speech to ease the pronunciation. Compare {{term|каланча|lang=ru}} for the same epenthesis.

